SS2022 singbridge: Close no longer releases the cached datagrams while ReadPacket uses them

FORK DEVIATION: a minimal fix, not upstream code. No upstream branch or tag fixes this race.
Upstream removed common/singbridge with the SS2022 refactor 65e853ed845e822b818386f0aeac93f5622dc41a
(#6831, first released in v26.9.30), which does not apply to the pin. sing's CopyPacketConn
closes both conns as soon as one copy direction ends, while the other direction can still be
inside ReadPacket, so Close released w.cached while ReadPacket split and replaced it: a data
race and a use of pooled buffers after their release. PacketConnWrapper now guards cached with
a mutex. Close marks the wrapper closed and releases what is cached; a ReadPacket after Close
returns io.ErrClosedPipe without reading the link; a read that returns from the link after
Close releases what it got instead of caching it; and concurrent reads merge into the cache
instead of replacing it. Applies after xray-ss2022-dispatch.patch, whose packet.go it extends.

